From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:01:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 061/107] power: supply: s2mpu06: count the charge cycles in
 the kernel

The fuel gauge adds up the drops of the state of charge (a hundred percent
is one cycle, jitter below half a percent is ignored) and keeps the result in
battery-backed NVMEM, which the RTC provides from its unused second alarm.
The cycle count is now read-only and selects the ageing step on its own.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4d0906027380566463561e1821a1e4d753da95df)
---
 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig             |   2 +
 drivers/power/supply/s2mpu06_fuelgauge.c | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 drivers/rtc/Kconfig                      |   4 +-
 drivers/rtc/rtc-s2mpu06.c                | 110 ++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 244 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
